\section{Strategic Recommendations}

Based on the comprehensive ESG analysis of PT AKR Corporindo Tbk (AKRA), several strategic recommendations can be formulated to enhance the company's sustainability performance while maintaining its competitive position in Indonesia's energy and logistics sectors.

\subsection{Environmental Strategy Enhancement}

AKRA should accelerate its transition toward renewable energy integration within its logistics operations. Given Indonesia's commitment to reducing carbon emissions by 29\% by 2030 under the Paris Agreement \cite{REF1}, AKRA can position itself as an industry leader by implementing solar-powered storage facilities and electric vehicle fleets for distribution. The company's existing infrastructure, including the Jakarta Tank Terminal (JTT) with its planned expansion to 350,000 KL capacity \cite{REF3}, provides an ideal platform for installing solar panels and energy storage systems.

The company should also explore opportunities in biofuel production and distribution, particularly given its existing capabilities in handling gasoline, fame, and biofuel \cite{REF3}. Indonesia's B30 biodiesel mandate presents a significant market opportunity that AKRA can leverage to diversify its product portfolio while contributing to national energy security goals.

\subsection{Social Responsibility Framework}

AKRA's joint venture with BP in retail fuel operations \cite{REF1} provides a unique opportunity to implement comprehensive community engagement programs. The company should establish local content requirements for its retail operations, prioritizing employment and procurement from local communities where its stations operate. This approach would align with Indonesia's localization policies while building stronger community relationships.

The company should also enhance its occupational health and safety standards across all operations, particularly in its logistics and storage facilities. Given the hazardous nature of petroleum products, implementing advanced safety protocols and regular employee training programs would demonstrate commitment to worker welfare while reducing operational risks.

\subsection{Governance and Transparency Improvements}

To strengthen its governance framework, AKRA should establish a dedicated sustainability committee within its board structure. This committee would oversee the implementation of ESG initiatives, monitor progress against targets, and ensure alignment with international best practices. The company's current financial strength, evidenced by its 37\% increase in net profit to Rp 1.64 trillion \cite{REF2}, provides the necessary resources to invest in comprehensive sustainability reporting and third-party verification.

AKRA should also enhance its stakeholder engagement processes by establishing regular dialogue with environmental groups, local communities, and government agencies. This proactive approach would help identify potential ESG risks early and demonstrate the company's commitment to responsible business practices.

\subsection{Supply Chain Sustainability}

Given AKRA's extensive logistics network and role as a key distributor of petroleum products, the company should implement a comprehensive supply chain sustainability program. This program should include supplier sustainability assessments, carbon footprint tracking for all logistics operations, and the development of circular economy initiatives for packaging and waste management.

The company's planned investment of US$ 45 million for JTT expansion \cite{REF3} presents an opportunity to incorporate sustainable design principles, including water recycling systems, energy-efficient lighting, and green building certification. These investments would not only reduce operational costs but also enhance the company's environmental credentials.

\subsection{Innovation and Technology Integration}

AKRA should invest in digital technologies to enhance its ESG performance. This includes implementing IoT sensors for real-time monitoring of storage facilities, blockchain technology for supply chain transparency, and AI-powered systems for optimizing logistics routes to reduce fuel consumption and emissions.

The company should also explore opportunities in emerging energy technologies, such as hydrogen fuel cells and energy storage systems, which could complement its existing petroleum business while positioning it for future energy transitions.

\subsection{Financial Sustainability Metrics}

To ensure the long-term viability of its ESG initiatives, AKRA should develop comprehensive sustainability-linked financial metrics. These could include tying executive compensation to ESG performance targets, establishing green bonds for funding sustainable projects, and creating internal carbon pricing mechanisms to guide investment decisions.

The company's strong financial position, with revenue growth of 29\% to Rp 23.55 trillion \cite{REF2}, provides the necessary foundation for these investments while maintaining shareholder returns.

By implementing these strategic recommendations, AKRA can enhance its ESG performance while maintaining its competitive position in Indonesia's energy and logistics sectors. These initiatives would not only contribute to national sustainability goals but also create long-term value for shareholders and stakeholders alike.
